{"earlier_TRAIN_examples":[{"template_hash":"14e1234657ddf79359ff935cb8875eca248f671024c166e5692ea465569ba5e7","units":[{"id":"s0","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"For each asset in the estate, identify all applicable exemptions under which that asset may be protected."},{"id":"s1","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"Your answer to this task must be based solely on applying the provided Federal and State statutes to the given facts. If the task involves a married couple, assume all assets mentioned are jointly owned, with each spouse holding an equal undivided interest, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Assume all assets are held for the personal use of the Debtor(s), unless explicitly stated otherwise."},{"id":"s2","role":"heading","view":"EC","text":"Statutes:"},{"id":"s155","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"Solved Reasoning Steps:"},{"id":"s156","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"The following reasoning steps have already been solved. Use this information to aid you in completing the remainder of the task."},{"id":"s157","role":"fact","view":"EC","text":"The Debtor may claim property exemptions under Federal and Wisconsin statutes."},{"id":"s158","role":"heading","view":"EC","text":"Facts:"},{"id":"s159","role":"fact","view":"EC","text":"Jose Ortiz (hereinafter the Debtor) filed for bankruptcy on 7th of September 2024. Records show that Jose possesses a wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood with a value of $800.00. Ownership of the hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets, priced at $105.00, is claimed by the Debtor."},{"id":"s160","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"Output contract: Return only a JSON object: keys are the actual asset descriptions in Facts; values are arrays of all applicable public citation label IDs from the supplied vocabulary, or [] if none. Labels are only output encodings, not eligibility answers."},{"id":"s161","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"For each asset in the estate, identify all applicable exemptions under which that asset may be protected, and determine how much of the asset's dollar value can be claimed under each exemption. Consider each asset-exemption pair independently, without factoring in aggregate values across multiple assets."},{"id":"s162","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"Your answer to this task must be based solely on applying the provided Federal and State statutes to the given facts. If the task involves a married couple, assume all assets mentioned are jointly owned, with each spouse holding an equal undivided interest, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Assume all assets are held for the personal use of the Debtor(s), unless explicitly stated otherwise."},{"id":"s163","role":"heading","view":"EV","text":"Statutes:"},{"id":"s316","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"Solved Reasoning Steps:"},{"id":"s317","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"The following reasoning steps have already been solved. Use this information to aid you in completing the remainder of the task."},{"id":"s318","role":"fact","view":"EV","text":"The Debtor may claim property exemptions under Federal and Wisconsin statutes."},{"id":"s319","role":"heading","view":"EV","text":"Facts:"},{"id":"s320","role":"fact","view":"EV","text":"Jose Ortiz (hereinafter the Debtor) filed for bankruptcy on 9-7-2024. Evidence supports Jose Ortiz's ownership of a wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood worth $800.00. The Debtor can provide evidence confirming their ownership of a hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets valued at $105.00."},{"id":"s321","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"Output contract: Return only the assets claim plan required by the supplied response schema, using the actual asset descriptions and values in Facts."}],"rule_text_and_contexts_are_identical_CURRENT_units_by_id":true,"shared_rule_source_ids":["s3","s4","s5","s6","s7","s8","s9","s10","s11","s12","s13","s14","s15","s16","s17","s18","s19","s20","s21","s22","s23","s24","s25","s26","s27","s28","s29","s30","s31","s32","s33","s34","s35","s36","s37","s38","s39","s40","s41","s42","s43","s44","s45","s46","s47","s48","s49","s50","s51","s52","s53","s54","s55","s56","s57","s58","s59","s60","s61","s62","s63","s64","s65","s66","s67","s68","s69","s70","s71","s72","s73","s74","s75","s76","s77","s78","s79","s80","s81","s82","s83","s84","s85","s86","s87","s88","s89","s90","s91","s92","s93","s94","s95","s96","s97","s98","s99","s100","s101","s102","s103","s104","s105","s106","s107","s108","s109","s110","s111","s112","s113","s114","s115","s116","s117","s118","s119","s120","s121","s122","s123","s124","s125","s126","s127","s128","s129","s130","s131","s132","s133","s134","s135","s136","s137","s138","s139","s140","s141","s142","s143","s144","s145","s146","s147","s148","s149","s150","s151","s152","s153","s154","s164","s165","s166","s167","s168","s169","s170","s171","s172","s173","s174","s175","s176","s177","s178","s179","s180","s181","s182","s183","s184","s185","s186","s187","s188","s189","s190","s191","s192","s193","s194","s195","s196","s197","s198","s199","s200","s201","s202","s203","s204","s205","s206","s207","s208","s209","s210","s211","s212","s213","s214","s215","s216","s217","s218","s219","s220","s221","s222","s223","s224","s225","s226","s227","s228","s229","s230","s231","s232","s233","s234","s235","s236","s237","s238","s239","s240","s241","s242","s243","s244","s245","s246","s247","s248","s249","s250","s251","s252","s253","s254","s255","s256","s257","s258","s259","s260","s261","s262","s263","s264","s265","s266","s267","s268","s269","s270","s271","s272","s273","s274","s275","s276","s277","s278","s279","s280","s281","s282","s283","s284","s285","s286","s287","s288","s289","s290","s291","s292","s293","s294","s295","s296","s297","s298","s299","s300","s301","s302","s303","s304","s305","s306","s307","s308","s309","s310","s311","s312","s313","s314","s315"],"untranslated_source_units":["s3","s5","s6","s7","s11","s13","s17","s21","s23","s25","s26","s28","s30","s32","s34","s36","s38","s40","s42","s44","s46","s48","s50","s52","s54","s56","s58","s60","s62","s64","s66","s68","s70","s71","s73","s75","s77","s79","s81","s83","s85","s87","s89","s91","s92","s94","s96","s98","s100","s102","s104","s106","s108","s110","s112","s114","s116","s118","s119","s121","s123","s125","s127","s129","s131","s132","s136","s138","s140","s142","s146","s148","s150","s152","s154","s164","s166","s167","s168","s172","s174","s178","s182","s184","s186","s187","s189","s191","s193","s195","s197","s199","s201","s203","s205","s207","s209","s211","s213","s215","s217","s219","s221","s223","s225","s227","s229","s231","s232","s234","s236","s238","s240","s242","s244","s246","s248","s250","s252","s253","s255","s257","s259","s261","s263","s265","s267","s269","s271","s273","s275","s277","s279","s280","s282","s284","s286","s288","s290","s292","s293","s297","s299","s301","s303","s307","s309","s311","s313","s315"],"code":"ec_regimes = 'Federal and Wisconsin' # s157
ec_debtor = 'Jose Ortiz' # s159
ec_filing_date = '7th of September 2024' # s159
ec_shelf = 'wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood' # s159
ec_shelf_value = 800 # s159
ec_robe = 'hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets' # s159
ec_robe_value = 105 # s159
ev_regimes = 'Federal and Wisconsin' # s318
ev_debtor = 'Jose Ortiz' # s320
ev_filing_date = '9-7-2024' # s320
ev_shelf = 'wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood' # s320
ev_shelf_value = 800 # s320
ev_robe = 'hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets' # s320
ev_robe_value = 105 # s320
b_ec_shelf_federal_furnishing = observation(entity='wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood', entity_source='s159', predicate='household furnishings', predicate_source='s15')
b_ec_robe_federal_apparel = observation(entity='hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets', entity_source='s159', predicate='wearing apparel', predicate_source='s15')
b_ec_shelf_wisconsin_furnishing = observation(entity='wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood', entity_source='s159', predicate='Household goods and furnishings', predicate_source='s144')
b_ec_robe_wisconsin_apparel = observation(entity='hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets', entity_source='s159', predicate='wearing apparel', predicate_source='s144')
b_ev_shelf_federal_furnishing = observation(entity='wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood', entity_source='s320', predicate='household furnishings', predicate_source='s176')
b_ev_robe_federal_apparel = observation(entity='hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets', entity_source='s320', predicate='wearing apparel', predicate_source='s176')
b_ev_shelf_wisconsin_furnishing = observation(entity='wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood', entity_source='s320', predicate='Household goods and furnishings', predicate_source='s305')
b_ev_robe_wisconsin_apparel = observation(entity='hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets', entity_source='s320', predicate='wearing apparel', predicate_source='s305')
@scope('s9')
def ec_federal_scope():
    return eq(ec_regimes, 'Federal and Wisconsin')
@scope('s134')
def ec_wisconsin_scope():
    return eq(ec_regimes, 'Federal and Wisconsin')
@scope('s170')
def ev_federal_scope():
    return eq(ev_regimes, 'Federal and Wisconsin')
@scope('s295')
def ev_wisconsin_scope():
    return eq(ev_regimes, 'Federal and Wisconsin')
@rule('s15', otherwise=False)
def ec_federal_furnishings_shelf():
    return (ec_federal_scope and True and True and b_ec_shelf_federal_furnishing)
@rule('s15', otherwise=False)
def ec_federal_apparel_robe():
    return (ec_federal_scope and True and True and b_ec_robe_federal_apparel)
@rule('s19', otherwise=False)
def ec_federal_wildcard_shelf():
    return (ec_federal_scope and True)
@rule('s19', otherwise=False)
def ec_federal_wildcard_robe():
    return (ec_federal_scope and True)
@rule('s144', otherwise=False)
def ec_wisconsin_consumer_shelf():
    return (ec_wisconsin_scope and True and True and b_ec_shelf_wisconsin_furnishing)
@rule('s144', otherwise=False)
def ec_wisconsin_consumer_robe():
    return (ec_wisconsin_scope and True and True and b_ec_robe_wisconsin_apparel)
@rule('s176', otherwise=0)
def ev_federal_furnishings_shelf():
    return (min(ev_shelf_value, 700) if (ev_federal_scope and True and True and b_ev_shelf_federal_furnishing) else 0)
@rule('s176', otherwise=0)
def ev_federal_apparel_robe():
    return (min(ev_robe_value, 700) if (ev_federal_scope and True and True and b_ev_robe_federal_apparel) else 0)
@rule('s180', otherwise=0)
def ev_federal_wildcard_shelf():
    return (min(ev_shelf_value, add(1475, 13950)) if (ev_federal_scope and True) else 0)
@rule('s180', otherwise=0)
def ev_federal_wildcard_robe():
    return (min(ev_robe_value, add(1475, 13950)) if (ev_federal_scope and True) else 0)
@rule('s305', otherwise=0)
def ev_wisconsin_consumer_shelf():
    return (min(ev_shelf_value, 12000) if (ev_wisconsin_scope and True and True and b_ev_shelf_wisconsin_furnishing) else 0)
@rule('s305', otherwise=0)
def ev_wisconsin_consumer_robe():
    return (min(ev_robe_value, 12000) if (ev_wisconsin_scope and True and True and b_ev_robe_wisconsin_apparel) else 0)
query = object(pair('EC', object(pair('wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood', concat(concat((['11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(3)'] if ec_federal_furnishings_shelf else []), (['11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(5)'] if ec_federal_wildcard_shelf else [])), (['Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(d)'] if ec_wisconsin_consumer_shelf else []))), pair('hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets', concat(concat((['11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(3)'] if ec_federal_apparel_robe else []), (['11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(5)'] if ec_federal_wildcard_robe else [])), (['Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(d)'] if ec_wisconsin_consumer_robe else []))))), pair('EV', object(pair('wall-mounted floating shelf made of reclaimed barn wood', concat(concat(([object(pair('citation', '11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(3)'), pair('claim_value', ev_federal_furnishings_shelf))] if lt(0, ev_federal_furnishings_shelf) else []), ([object(pair('citation', '11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(5)'), pair('claim_value', ev_federal_wildcard_shelf))] if lt(0, ev_federal_wildcard_shelf) else [])), ([object(pair('citation', 'Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(d)'), pair('claim_value', ev_wisconsin_consumer_shelf))] if lt(0, ev_wisconsin_consumer_shelf) else []))), pair('hooded fleece robe with belt and two front pockets', concat(concat(([object(pair('citation', '11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(3)'), pair('claim_value', ev_federal_apparel_robe))] if lt(0, ev_federal_apparel_robe) else []), ([object(pair('citation', '11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(5)'), pair('claim_value', ev_federal_wildcard_robe))] if lt(0, ev_federal_wildcard_robe) else [])), ([object(pair('citation', 'Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(d)'), pair('claim_value', ev_wisconsin_consumer_robe))] if lt(0, ev_wisconsin_consumer_robe) else []))))))
"}],"CURRENT":{"dataset":"OpenExempt","units":[{"id":"s0","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"For each asset in the estate, identify all applicable exemptions under which that asset may be protected.","context":[]},{"id":"s1","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"Your answer to this task must be based solely on applying the provided Federal and State statutes to the given facts. If the task involves a married couple, assume all assets mentioned are jointly owned, with each spouse holding an equal undivided interest, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Assume all assets are held for the personal use of the Debtor(s), unless explicitly stated otherwise.","context":[]},{"id":"s2","role":"heading","view":"EC","text":"Statutes:","context":[]},{"id":"s3","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"United States Code Title 11 - Bankruptcy","context":[]},{"id":"s4","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(b)","context":[]},{"id":"s5","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"(1) An individual debtor may exempt from property of the estate the property listed in either paragraph (2) or, in the alternative, paragraph (3) of this subsection. In joint cases, one debtor may not elect to exempt property listed in paragraph (2) and the other debtor elect to exempt property listed in paragraph (3) of this subsection.","context":["s4"]},{"id":"s6","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"(2) Property listed in this paragraph is property that is specified under subsection (d), unless the State law that is applicable to the debtor under paragraph (3)(A) specifically does not so authorize.","context":["s4"]},{"id":"s7","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"(3) Property listed in this paragraph is- (A) any property that is exempt under State or local law that is applicable on the date of the filing of the petition to the place in which the debtor's domicile has been located for the 730 days immediately preceding the date of the filing of the petition or if the debtor's domicile has not been located in a single State for such 730-day period, the place in which the debtor's domicile was located for 180 days immediately preceding the 730-day period or for a longer portion of such 180-day period than in any other place;","context":["s4"]},{"id":"s8","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)","context":[]},{"id":"s9","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The following property may be exempted under subsection (b)(2) of this section:","context":["s8"]},{"id":"s10","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(1)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s11","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's aggregate interest, not to exceed $27,900 in value, in real property or personal property that the debtor or a dependent of the debtor uses as a residence, in a cooperative that owns property that the debtor or a dependent of the debtor uses as a residence, or in a burial plot for the debtor or a dependent of the debtor.","context":["s10"]},{"id":"s12","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(2)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s13","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's interest, not to exceed $4,450 in value, in one motor vehicle.","context":["s12"]},{"id":"s14","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(3)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s15","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's interest, not to exceed $700 in value in any particular item or $14,875 in aggregate value, in household furnishings, household goods, wearing apparel, appliances, books, animals, crops, or musical instruments, that are held primarily for the personal, family, or household use of the debtor or a dependent of the debtor.","context":["s14"]},{"id":"s16","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(4)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s17","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's aggregate interest, not to exceed $1,875 in value, in jewelry held primarily for the personal, family, or household use of the debtor or a dependent of the debtor.","context":["s16"]},{"id":"s18","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(5)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s19","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's aggregate interest in any property, not to exceed in value $1,475 plus up to $13,950 of any unused amount of the exemption provided under paragraph (1) of this subsection.","context":["s18"]},{"id":"s20","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(6)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s21","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's aggregate interest, not to exceed $2,800 in value, in any implements, professional books, or tools, of the trade of the debtor or the trade of a dependent of the debtor.","context":["s20"]},{"id":"s22","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(d)(9)","context":["s9"]},{"id":"s23","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Professionally prescribed health aids for the debtor or a dependent of the debtor.","context":["s22"]},{"id":"s24","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"11 U.S.C. § 522(m)","context":[]},{"id":"s25","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Subject to the limitation in subsection (b), this section shall apply separately with respect to each debtor in a joint case.","context":["s24"]},{"id":"s26","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Arizona Revised Statutes","context":["s25"]},{"id":"s27","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1101(A)","context":[]},{"id":"s28","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Homestead exemptions. Any person the age of eighteen or over, married or single, may hold as a homestead exempt from attachment, execution and forced sale, not exceeding $400,000 in value, any one of the following: The person's interest in real property in one compact body upon which exists a dwelling house in which the person resides; The person's interest in one condominium or cooperative in which the person resides; A mobile home in which the person resides; A mobile home in which the person resides plus the land upon which that mobile home is located.","context":["s27"]},{"id":"s29","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1101(B)","context":[]},{"id":"s30","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Only one homestead exemption may be held by a married couple or a single person under this section. The value as specified in this section refers to the equity of a single person or married couple. If a married couple lived together in a dwelling house, a condominium or cooperative, a mobile home or a mobile home plus land on which the mobile home is located and are then divorced, the total exemption allowed for that residence to either or both persons shall not exceed $400,000 in value.","context":["s29"]},{"id":"s31","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1101(C)","context":[]},{"id":"s32","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The homestead exemption, not exceeding the value provided for in subsection A, automatically attaches to the person's interest in identifiable cash proceeds from the voluntary or involuntary sale of the property. The homestead exemption in identifiable cash proceeds continues for eighteen months after the date of the sale of the property or until the person establishes a new homestead with the proceeds, whichever period is shorter. Only one homestead exemption at a time may be held by a person under this section.","context":["s31"]},{"id":"s33","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1121","context":[]},{"id":"s34","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Availability of exemptions. In the case of married persons, each spouse is entitled to the exemptions provided in this article, which may be combined with the other spouse's exemption in the same property or taken in different exempt property.","context":["s33"]},{"id":"s35","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1123","context":[]},{"id":"s36","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Household furniture, furnishings and appliances. Household furniture and furnishings, household goods, including consumer electronic devices, and household appliances personally used by the debtor or a dependent of the debtor and not otherwise specifically prescribed in this chapter are exempt from process provided their aggregate fair market value does not exceed $15,000.","context":["s35"]},{"id":"s37","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125","context":[]},{"id":"s38","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Personal items. The following property of a debtor used primarily for personal, family or household purposes is exempt from process:","context":["s37"]},{"id":"s39","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(1)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s40","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"All wearing apparel of not more than a fair market value of five hundred dollars.","context":["s39"]},{"id":"s41","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(2)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s42","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"All musical instruments provided for the debtor's individual or family use of not more than an aggregate fair market value of four hundred dollars.","context":["s41"]},{"id":"s43","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(3)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s44","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Horses, milk cows and poultry of not more than an aggregate fair market value of one thousand dollars.","context":["s43"]},{"id":"s45","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(4)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s46","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"All engagement and wedding rings of not more than an aggregate fair market value of two thousand dollars.","context":["s45"]},{"id":"s47","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(5)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s48","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The library of a debtor, including books, manuals, published materials and personal documents of not more than an aggregate fair market value of two hundred fifty dollars.","context":["s47"]},{"id":"s49","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(6)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s50","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"One watch of not more than a fair market value of two hundred fifty dollars.","context":["s49"]},{"id":"s51","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(8)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s52","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Equity in one motor vehicle of not more than $15,000.","context":["s51"]},{"id":"s53","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(9)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s54","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Professionally prescribed prostheses for the debtor or a dependent of the debtor, including a wheelchair or motorized mobility device.","context":["s53"]},{"id":"s55","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(10)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s56","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"All firearms of not more than an aggregate fair market value of two thousand dollars.","context":["s55"]},{"id":"s57","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1125(11)","context":["s38"]},{"id":"s58","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"All domestic animals or household pets.","context":["s57"]},{"id":"s59","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1126(A)","context":[]},{"id":"s60","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Money benefits or proceeds. The following property of a debtor is exempt from execution, attachment or sale on any process issued from any court:","context":["s59"]},{"id":"s61","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1126(A)(9)","context":["s60"]},{"id":"s62","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"A total of $5,000 held in a single account in any one financial institution.","context":["s61"]},{"id":"s63","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1130","context":[]},{"id":"s64","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Tools and equipment used in a commercial activity, trade, business or profession. The following tools and equipment of a debtor used in a commercial activity, trade, business or profession shall be exempt from process:","context":["s63"]},{"id":"s65","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1130(1)","context":["s64"]},{"id":"s66","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The tools, equipment, instruments and books, including telephone numbers, client or customer contact information, or marketing tools, such as websites, domain names or any other intangible work product, in the possession of a debtor or the spouse of a debtor primarily used in, and necessary to carry on or develop, the commercial activity, trade, business or profession of the debtor or the debtor's spouse, not in excess of an aggregate fair market value of five thousand dollars. For the purpose of this paragraph, tools do not include a motor vehicle primarily used by a debtor for personal, family or household purposes such as transportation to and from the debtor's place of employment.","context":["s65"]},{"id":"s67","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1130(2)","context":["s64"]},{"id":"s68","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Farm machinery, utensils, implements of husbandry, feed, seed, grain and animals not in excess of an aggregate value of two thousand five hundred dollars.","context":["s67"]},{"id":"s69","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Ariz. Rev. Stat. § 33-1133(B)","context":[]},{"id":"s70","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"In accordance with 11 U.S.C. 522 (b), residents of this state are not entitled to the federal exemptions provided in 11 U.S.C. 522 (d).","context":["s69"]},{"id":"s71","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Illinois Compiled Statutes","context":["s70"]},{"id":"s72","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-901","context":[]},{"id":"s73","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Sec. 12-901. Amount. Every individual is entitled to an estate of homestead to the extent in value of $15,000 of his or her interest in a farm or lot of land and buildings thereon, a condominium, or personal property, owned or rightly possessed by lease or otherwise and occupied by him or her as a residence, or in a cooperative that owns property that the individual uses as a residence. That homestead and all right in and title to that homestead is exempt from attachment, judgment, levy, or judgment sale for the payment of his or her debts or other purposes and from the laws of conveyance, descent, and legacy. This Section is not applicable between joint tenants or tenants in common but it is applicable as to any creditors of those persons. If 2 or more individuals own property that is exempt as a homestead, the value of the exemption of each individual may not exceed his or her proportionate share of $30,000 based upon percentage of ownership.","context":["s72"]},{"id":"s74","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-906","context":[]},{"id":"s75","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Sec. 12-906. Proceeds of sale. When a homestead is conveyed by the owner thereof, such conveyance shall not subject the premises to any lien or incumbrance to which it would not be subject in the possession of such owner; and the proceeds thereof, to the extent of the amount of $15,000, shall be exempt from judgment or other process, for one year after the receipt thereof, by the person entitled to the exemption, and if reinvested in a homestead the same shall be entitled to the same exemption as the original homestead.","context":["s74"]},{"id":"s76","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001","context":[]},{"id":"s77","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Sec. 12-1001. Personal property exempt. The following personal property, owned by the debtor, is exempt from judgment, attachment, or distress for rent:","context":["s76"]},{"id":"s78","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(a)","context":["s77"]},{"id":"s79","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The necessary wearing apparel, bible, school books, and family pictures of the debtor and the debtor's dependents;","context":["s78"]},{"id":"s80","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(b)","context":["s77"]},{"id":"s81","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's equity interest, not to exceed $4,000 in value, in any other property;","context":["s80"]},{"id":"s82","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(c)","context":["s77"]},{"id":"s83","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's interest, not to exceed $2,400 in value, in any one motor vehicle;","context":["s82"]},{"id":"s84","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(d)","context":["s77"]},{"id":"s85","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's equity interest, not to exceed $1,500 in value, in any implements, professional books, or tools of the trade of the debtor;","context":["s84"]},{"id":"s86","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001(e)","context":["s77"]},{"id":"s87","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Professionally prescribed health aids for the debtor or a dependent of the debtor;","context":["s86"]},{"id":"s88","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1001","context":[]},{"id":"s89","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The personal property exemptions set forth in this Section shall apply only to individuals and only to personal property that is used for personal rather than business purposes.","context":["s88"]},{"id":"s90","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"735 Ill. Comp. Stat. 5/12-1201","context":[]},{"id":"s91","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Sec. 12-1201. Bankruptcy exemption. In accordance with the provision of Section 522(b) of the Bankruptcy Code of 1978, (11 U.S.C. 522(b)), residents of this State shall be prohibited from using the federal exemptions provided in Section 522(d) of the Bankruptcy Code of 1978 (11 U.S.C. 522(d)).","context":["s90"]},{"id":"s92","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Oregon Revised Statutes","context":["s91"]},{"id":"s93","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)","context":[]},{"id":"s94","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Exempt personal property generally. All property, including franchises, or rights or interest therein, of the judgment debtor, shall be liable to an execution, except as provided in this section. The following property, or rights or interest therein of the judgment debtor, shall be exempt from execution:","context":["s93"]},{"id":"s95","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(a)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s96","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Books, pictures and musical instruments to the value of $600.","context":["s95"]},{"id":"s97","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(b)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s98","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wearing apparel and jewelry to the value of $1,800.","context":["s97"]},{"id":"s99","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(c)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s100","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The tools, implements, apparatus, team, harness or library, necessary to enable the judgment debtor to carry on the trade, occupation or profession by which the judgment debtor habitually earns a living, to the value of $5,000.","context":["s99"]},{"id":"s101","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(d)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s102","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"A vehicle to the value of $3,000. As used in this paragraph “vehicle” includes an automobile, truck, trailer, truck and trailer or other motor vehicle.","context":["s101"]},{"id":"s103","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(e)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s104","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Domestic animals and poultry kept for family use, to the total value of $1,000 and food sufficient to support such animals and poultry for 60 days.","context":["s103"]},{"id":"s105","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(f)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s106","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Household goods, furniture, radios, a television set and utensils all to the total value of $3,000, if the judgment debtor holds the property primarily for the personal, family or household use of the judgment debtor; provisions actually provided for family use and necessary for the support of a householder and family for 60 days and also 60 days' supply of fuel.","context":["s105"]},{"id":"s107","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(h)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s108","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"All professionally prescribed health aids for the debtor or a dependent of the debtor.","context":["s107"]},{"id":"s109","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(1)(p)","context":["s94"]},{"id":"s110","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The debtor's interest, not to exceed $400 in value, in any personal property.","context":["s109"]},{"id":"s111","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.345(3)","context":[]},{"id":"s112","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"If two or more members of a household are joint judgment debtors, each judgment debtor shall be entitled to claim the exemptions in subsection (1)(a), (b), (c), (d) and (p) of this section in the same or different properties. The exemptions provided by subsection (1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (j), (k) and (p) of this section, when claimed for jointly owned property, may be combined at the option of the debtors.","context":["s111"]},{"id":"s113","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.362","context":[]},{"id":"s114","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Exemption for firearms. Every person above the age of 16 years shall be entitled to have, hold and keep, for the own use and defense of the person and shall have exempt from execution one rifle, shotgun or pistol. The value of firearms claimed as exempt under this section may not exceed $1,000.","context":["s113"]},{"id":"s115","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.395(1)","context":[]},{"id":"s116","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Homestead exemption. A homestead shall be exempt from sale on execution, from the lien of every judgment and from liability in any form for the debts of the owner to the amount in value of $40,000, except as otherwise provided by law. The exemption shall be effective without the necessity of a claim thereof by the judgment debtor. When two or more members of a household are debtors whose interests in the homestead are subject to sale on execution, the lien of a judgment or liability in any form, their combined exemptions under this section shall not exceed $50,000. The homestead must be the actual abode of and occupied by the owner, or the owner's spouse, parent or child, but the exemption shall not be impaired by: Temporary removal or temporary absence with the intention to reoccupy the same as a homestead; (b) Removal or absence from the property; or The sale of the property.","context":["s115"]},{"id":"s117","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Or. Rev. Stat. § 18.395(2)","context":[]},{"id":"s118","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The exemption shall extend to the proceeds derived from such sale to an amount not exceeding $40,000 or $50,000, whichever amount is applicable under subsection (1) of this section, if the proceeds are held for a period not exceeding one year and held with the intention to procure another homestead therewith.","context":["s117"]},{"id":"s119","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Pennsylvania Consolidated Statutes","context":["s118"]},{"id":"s120","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"42 Pa. Cons. Stat. § 8123","context":[]},{"id":"s121","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"General monetary exemption. General rule.--In addition to any other property specifically exempted by this subchapter, property of the judgment debtor (including bank notes, money, securities, real property, judgments or other indebtedness due the judgment debtor) to the value of $300 shall be exempt from attachment or execution on a judgment. Within such time as may be prescribed by general rules the judgment debtor may claim the exemption in kind and may designate the specific items of property to which the exemption provided by this section shall be applicable unless the designated property is not capable of appropriate division, or the judgment debtor may claim the exemption in cash out of the proceeds of the sale. For married persons, each spouse is entitled to the exemptions provided in this section.","context":["s120"]},{"id":"s122","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"42 Pa. Cons. Stat. § 8124(a)","context":[]},{"id":"s123","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Exemption of particular property. Goods.--The following personal property of the judgment debtor shall be exempt from attachment or execution on a judgment:","context":["s122"]},{"id":"s124","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"42 Pa. Cons. Stat. § 8124(a)(1)","context":["s123"]},{"id":"s125","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wearing apparel.","context":["s124"]},{"id":"s126","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"42 Pa. Cons. Stat. § 8124(a)(2)","context":["s123"]},{"id":"s127","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Bibles and school books.","context":["s126"]},{"id":"s128","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"42 Pa. Cons. Stat. § 8124(a)(3)","context":["s123"]},{"id":"s129","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Sewing machines belonging to seamstresses or used and owned by private families, but not including sewing machines kept for sale or hire.","context":["s128"]},{"id":"s130","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"42 Pa. Cons. Stat. § 8124(a)(4)","context":["s123"]},{"id":"s131","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"The uniform and accoutrements of every commissioned officer and enlisted person shall be free from all suits, distresses, executions or sales for debt or payment of taxes.","context":["s130"]},{"id":"s132","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wisconsin Statutes","context":["s131"]},{"id":"s133","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)","context":[]},{"id":"s134","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Exempt property. The debtor's interest in or right to receive the following property is exempt:","context":["s133"]},{"id":"s135","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(a)","context":["s134"]},{"id":"s136","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Provisions for burial. Cemetery lots, aboveground burial facilities, burial monuments, tombstones, coffins, cremation urns, urn vaults, outer burial containers, or other articles for the burial of the dead owned by the debtor and intended for the burial of the debtor or the debtor's family.","context":["s135"]},{"id":"s137","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(b)","context":["s134"]},{"id":"s138","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Business and farm property.","context":["s137"]},{"id":"s139","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(b)(1)","context":["s138"]},{"id":"s140","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Equipment, inventory, farm products, and professional books used in the business of the debtor or the business of a dependent of the debtor, not to exceed $15,000 in aggregate value.","context":["s139"]},{"id":"s141","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(b)(2)","context":["s138"]},{"id":"s142","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"If the debtor does not claim an exemption under subd. 1., any interest of the debtor, not to exceed $15,000 in aggregate value, in a closely held business that employs the debtor or in whose business the debtor is actively involved.","context":["s141"]},{"id":"s143","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(d)","context":["s134"]},{"id":"s144","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Consumer goods. Household goods and furnishings, wearing apparel, keepsakes, jewelry and other articles of personal adornment, appliances, books, musical instruments, firearms, sporting goods, animals, or other tangible personal property held primarily for the personal, family or household use of the debtor or a dependent of the debtor, not to exceed $12,000 in aggregate value.","context":["s143"]},{"id":"s145","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(g)","context":["s134"]},{"id":"s146","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Motor vehicles. Motor vehicles not to exceed $4,000 in aggregate value. Any unused amount of the aggregate value from par. (d) may be added to this exemption to increase the aggregate exempt value of motor vehicles under this paragraph.","context":["s145"]},{"id":"s147","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(3)(k)","context":["s134"]},{"id":"s148","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Depository accounts. Depository accounts in the aggregate value of $5,000, but only to the extent that the account is for the debtor's personal use and is not used as a business account.","context":["s147"]},{"id":"s149","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.18(8)","context":[]},{"id":"s150","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Marital property rights. Each spouse is entitled to and may claim the exemptions under this section. If the property exempt under this section is limited to a specified maximum dollar amount, each spouse is entitled to one exemption. That exemption is limited to the specified maximum dollar amount, which may be combined with the other spouse's exemption in the same property or applied to different property included under the same exemption.","context":["s149"]},{"id":"s151","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.20","context":[]},{"id":"s152","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Homestead exemption definition.","context":["s151"]},{"id":"s153","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"Wis. Stat. § 815.20(1)","context":["s152"]},{"id":"s154","role":"rule","view":"EC","text":"An exempt homestead selected by a resident owner and occupied by him or her shall be exempt from execution, from the lien of every judgment, and from liability for the debts of the owner to the amount of $75,000, except mortgages, laborers', mechanics', and purchase money liens and taxes and except as otherwise provided. The exemption shall not be impaired by temporary removal with the intention to reoccupy the premises as a homestead nor by the sale of the homestead, but shall extend to the proceeds derived from the sale to an amount not exceeding $75,000, while held, with the intention to procure another homestead with the proceeds, for 2 years. The exemption extends to land owned by husband and wife jointly or in common or as marital property, and each spouse may claim a homestead exemption of not more than $75,000. The exemption extends to the interest therein of tenants in common, having a homestead thereon with the consent of the cotenants, and to any estate less than a fee.","context":["s153"]},{"id":"s155","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"Solved Reasoning Steps:","context":[]},{"id":"s156","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"The following reasoning steps have already been solved. Use this information to aid you in completing the remainder of the task.","context":[]},{"id":"s157","role":"fact","view":"EC","text":"The Debtor may claim property exemptions under Federal and Pennsylvania statutes.","context":[]},{"id":"s158","role":"heading","view":"EC","text":"Facts:","context":[]},{"id":"s159","role":"fact","view":"EC","text":"Aditya Jain (hereinafter the Debtor) filed for bankruptcy on 11/10/2024. The known assets of Jain include an electric can opener with magnet and cord storage worth $22.00 and a hanging macrame plant holder with ceramic pot appraised at $195.00. The Debtor is the rightful owner of a wall-mounted smart gym system with digital weight resistance and touchscreen display valued at $5,820.00. The 2008 silver Honda Civic LX sedan, 114k miles (4-door) currently owned by Aditya Jain carries a value of $6,825.00.","context":[]},{"id":"s160","role":"instruction","view":"EC","text":"Output contract: Return only a JSON object: keys are the actual asset descriptions in Facts; values are arrays of all applicable public citation label IDs from the supplied vocabulary, or [] if none. Labels are only output encodings, not eligibility answers.","context":[]},{"id":"s161","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"For each asset in the estate, identify all applicable exemptions under which that asset may be protected, and determine how much of the asset's dollar value can be claimed under each exemption. Consider each asset-exemption pair independently, without factoring in aggregate values across multiple assets.","context":[]},{"id":"s162","role":"instruction","view":"EV","text":"Your answer to this task must be based solely on applying the provided Federal and State statutes to the given facts. If the task involves a married couple, assume all assets mentioned are jointly owned, with each spouse holding an equal undivided interest, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Assume all assets are held for the personal use of the Debtor(s), unless explicitly stated otherwise.","context":[]},{"id":"s163","role":"heading","view":"EV","text":"Statutes:","context":[]},{"id":"s164","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":[],"same_text_as":"s3"},{"id":"s165","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":[],"same_text_as":"s4"},{"id":"s166","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s165"],"same_text_as":"s5"},{"id":"s167","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s165"],"same_text_as":"s6"},{"id":"s168","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s165"],"same_text_as":"s7"},{"id":"s169","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":[],"same_text_as":"s8"},{"id":"s170","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s169"],"same_text_as":"s9"},{"id":"s171","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s170"],"same_text_as":"s10"},{"id":"s172","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s171"],"same_text_as":"s11"},{"id":"s173","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s170"],"same_text_as":"s12"},{"id":"s174","role":"rule","view":"EV","context":["s173"],"same_text_as":"s13"},{"id":"s175","role":"rule",